**Key Areas of Concern**

**1. Accessibility ****&**** Inclusion (Digital Health) — Urgent Across All Areas**

Portfolio average: 3.0/5. This is the weakest dimension across all 20 areas. No area has WCAG 2.2 AA practice embedded, proactive AT offer, or Accessibility Checker use as standard. HBH/EYE (score 2) and English (score 2) are the most critical. Computing, Engineering, Pre-Employment, Sport, FE Counselling score 3–4 in terms of awareness but not systematic practice.

**Action:**

- Accessibility Teach-Meet — schedule before September. Content: WCAG 2.2 AA basics, Immersive Reader demo, Live Captions, alt text, accessible assignment design, Accessibility Checker walkthrough.

- Priority attendees: HBH/EYE (Tracey & Sharon to co-facilitate post-training), English (Libby/Georgie), Maths (Jason/confirmed DL), Motor Vehicle (Ben Holt).

- Post-Teach-Meet: 1:1 follow-up with each area within 2 weeks to agree one specific accessibility commitment.

**2. Digital Skills Baseline Assessment — Not Embedded Anywhere**

Portfolio average: 3.1/5. English explicitly states "No" to baseline assessment. Motor Vehicle has no formal method. Sport only partially assessed. Pre-Employment needs an adult-specific literacy IA. Most areas assess digital skills implicitly within qualification units rather than through dedicated digital IA.

**Action:**

- Quick win: By September, all 20 areas to have confirmed a method for baseline-assessing learner digital skills — even if it is as simple as the Century IA plus a one-question self-assessment.

- Specialist digital skills rubrics: target 1 rubric drafted per area by October half-term, piloted in one unit.

**3. Device ****&**** Infrastructure Gaps — Blocking Practice in Key Areas**

FEH: Library laptops slow and unreliable; LapSafe plans submitted — follow up urgently. Engineering: Device impact rated 1 (significant); lecture capture inadequate; software licensing not apprentice-friendly. FE Counselling: Whiteboard failures for 2+ years — formal escalation needed. Protective Services: PC battery issues; WiFi effectiveness. GMA: WiFi "challenging"; no IT on site.

**Action:**

- Escalate FEH LapSafe approval timeline — this is blocking daily teaching.

- Engineering device and lecture capture proposal — support Thanos in building the business case for senior leadership.

- GMA WiFi and IT on-site request — pass to Joe A/IT with specific rooms and frequency of impact.

- FE Counselling whiteboard replacement — this has been ongoing for 2+ years; it needs a formal written complaint escalation.

**4. HoA Leadership ****&**** Strategic Planning — Variable Ownership**

Portfolio average: 3.5/5. No area has a written digital QIP target. Computing and Engineering score 5 and 4 respectively — exemplary. BUS, CON, Sixth Form, PRS score 3 — aware but no formal plan. PRS and Motor Vehicle submitted by staff who are not the HoA.

**Action:**

- Coaching conversations with all 20 HoAs — use this document as the conversation-starter.

- By September: each area to articulate top 3 digital priorities for the coming year.

- By October: digital priority referenced in at least one QIP target per area.

**5. Digital Lead Gaps — Three Unresolved**

- BUS: "TBC – sorry!" — no DL confirmed despite positive HoA engagement.

- PRS: DL listed as "Graham Wright" — this is Graeme (the DPC). Misidentification. Louise to nominate within her own team.

- MAT: Three names proposed (Denholm Wilcox, Diego Fanhe, Joel Baylis). No decision made. HoA to resolve this week.

**Detailed Area Assessments**

Scores are derived from audit evidence only. Where a dimension is scored, the basis for that score is noted. Where evidence is insufficient, the cell is left blank rather than estimated. This preserves accuracy — a gap is more useful than a guess.

All scores use the new 8-dimension framework: 1 = Urgent · 2 = Challenged · 3 = Developing · 4 = On Track · 5 = Confident. Scores are weighted averages of sub-criteria where rated.

**BUS · Business and Travel (BUS)**

**HoA: **Ben Melhuish**   DL: **TBC (not yet confirmed)**   Overall: ****3.3 · Developing**

| **Dimension** | **Score** | **Basis for rating** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Staff Digital Capability ****&**** Confidence** | **4 · On Track** | Staff confident with AI, PM tools, dashboards (self-reported). Less confident with CRM/booking systems (GDS/OTA). |
| **HoA Leadership, Planning ****&**** Strategy** | **3 · Developing** | Positive conversations; DL not yet confirmed ("TBC – sorry!"). No written digital plan. |
| **Infrastructure ****&**** Devices** | **4 · On Track** | 417/420 combined PCs — strong bank. Some equity gaps (non-bursary learners without laptops). |
| **Digital Skills Assessment ****&**** Tracking** | **3 · Developing** | AI and PM assessed within units. CRM, booking, and digital comms need broader coverage. |
| **Digital Curriculum Integration** | **3 · Developing** | Clear sector skills pathway. CRM/booking integration not yet systematic. |
| **Learner Readiness ****&**** Digital Confidence** | **3 · Developing** | Some learners without laptops who don't qualify for access-to-tech scheme. |
| **Digital Health (Accessibility ****&**** Inclusion)** | **3 · Developing** | Read&Write used including in exams. No systematic accessibility practice evident. |
| **Digital Lead Engagement ****&**** Health Checks** | **3 · Developing** | DL not confirmed ("TBC – sorry!"). HoA engaged but DL role not yet filled. |

**Rationale:**

On Track overall. Strong device infrastructure and staff AI/PM capability. CRM and Digital Booking Systems are explicit gaps. DL confirmation is the immediate unlock. Accessibility training needed but not a critical blocker.

**Context — General ****&**** Industry Digital Skills, Staff Confidence:**

General digital skills: Data/dashboard management, CRM systems, project management tools, digital communications, AI literacy. Travel-specific: GDS (Global Distribution Systems), OTA (Online Travel Agency) platforms, digital booking systems. Software barrier rated moderate (score 2). Staff capability barrier rated low (score 4). Devices: Strong bank of 417/420 combined PCs at Knightstone.

**Strengths:**

- Strong and well-resourced device bank.

- Staff confident with AI, PM tools, and dashboards.

- Teams class spaces well-utilised.

- Clear digital skills pathway for the sector.

- Read&Write in use including in exams.

- Positive HoA engagement.

**AFI Phases — Structured Immediate Actions:**

- Phase 1: Confirm and induct Digital Lead. Agree DL role and first activity.

- Phase 2: 100% Century IA completion. CRM barrier audit — identify which platform to pilot and what licensing would require.

- Phase 2–3: Accessibility Teach-Meet participation. AT showcase for staff.

- Phase 3: Pilot CRM/booking platform training. Specialist skills rubric drafted for Travel and Business units.

**BUI/CON · Construction Building Services Motor Vehicle**

